abstract: >
  Beginner-friendly talk and hands-on examples for molecular simulation:
  what it is, why it works (statistical mechanics → ensembles), and how to
  run one (potentials, integrators, thermostats, analysis). Pure-Python
  runnable examples plus optional OpenMM/ASE extensions.
